SCP-5234 shown and hung before containment.



Item #:  SCP-5234

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5234 resides in a compact box consisting of concrete, set on a table in a soundproof room in site-19. Scp-5234 is to be tied up with any sort of bonded material such as fiber or elastic rope when not in examination. Research and inspection checks are to be made when SCP-5234 has consumed enough matter to increase or exceed above its average size, or when recent developments and info have been made regarding SCP-5234. SCP-5234 should never be removed from its containment for any other reason than testing or research purposes. Only researchers with clearance level 3 or higher are allowed within the confinement of the anomaly’s cell. During an inspection, standard earplugs, as well as protective equipment: such as class-A hazmat suits, must be worn during the process.

If SCP-5234 is seen or noted replicating appendages, limbs; or any extremities that were once part of SCP-5234-A such as eyes, arms, veins, hair or legs. Then the immediate lockdown of SCP-5234's cell will commence. With the addition of two armed guards to be stationed outside of the containment chamber until SCP-5234 is starved enough were re-containment inside SCP-5234’s box is plausible. SCP-5234's extra exterminates will deteriorate over a period of time without the consistency of sustaining itself. SCP-5234 can manipulate and move these limbs seemingly with apparent ease. Scp-5234’s main goal seems to consist of blending in as seamlessly as possible with the former exception of any or all extra extremities that can break the illusion of Scp-5234’s disguise.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Description:  SCP-5234 is a 3m radius of SCP-5234 that hear the whispers undergo a hypnotic and frenzied state.1 If SCP-5234 comes into contact with skin or any exposed part of the body, the person in question who has made initial contact with SCP-5234 is to be marked as SCP-5234-A. While the appendage or limb that’s stuck is to be amputated immediately. Salvaging as much as possible off of SCP-5234 to avoid the further feeding and development of SCP-5234. If the torso, head, and or more than three appendages are stuck to SCP-5234, then an immediate termination of SCP-5234-A is put into effect. Alongside the salvaging and cremation of any leftover body parts stuck to SCP-5234. After a period of one (1) to three (3) days, if SCP-5234-A hasn’t freed themselves from contact (or died from natural causes) The following anomalies' effects will begin to take place.

SCP-XXX-A’s skin, blood, flesh, and veins will begin to deteriorate into the curtain discarding only bone. Rapidly succumbing to blood loss shortly after.2
SCP-5234-A will start to give off a unusual odor, consistent with the subject's last eaten meal. Or In rare cases may give off an odor consistent too ████.
If SCP-5234-A is forcefully separated from SCP-5234 by an outside force at any time, SCP-5234-A will become aggressive and irritable until given class-A amnestics or reunited with SCP-5234.


If enough human matter equivalent to SCP-5234’s current size and weight is consumed within a recorded one (1) to two (2) day period, extra extremities will begin to grow from SCP-5234 that includes: hair, multiple sets of eyes, legs, arms or hands, noses and ears. SCP-5234 has noted to adapt to the situation it is currently faced with when consuming matter. When in this state, SCP-5234 can enhance all senses which include: smell, hearing, vision, taste, and touch. SCP-5234 seems to be able to manipulate and move these limbs around itself to better blend in and close distance between itself and its target.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Addendum:  Signs of SCP-5234 first came to light when reports that an unknown shapeless entity had plummeted from the sky, right before the reported deaths of 225 people in Champagne Illinois on 7/27/2005 (Stated below).


Discovery.5234 
Due to a three day period of silence designated from 7/27/2005 - 7/30/2005, 225 reports of civilian deaths were filled by Champagne Illinois to the Foundation, following the sighting of SCP-5234. As an immediate response to this unusual jump and spike of numbers. The Foundation took interest and shut out every entrance into this town, making it a priority that no one enters or leaves the surrounding area. Soon after an exploration into the town. Several samples of decalcified skulls, bones, hair, and SCP-5234 were recovered. Scp-5234 was noted in the phase of growth and developing in the husk of a middle-aged man who still hasn’t been identified as of yet when recovered. SCP-5234 was seen using this husk as a way to disguise and move around the town freely consuming matter, equivalent enough to produce limbs and perform its anomaly’s abilities. The husk of this man was discovered after SCP-5234 had unraveled from this husk and ambushed MTF Epsilon-6 units.3 Commander Linwood ruled nothing could be done beyond the starvation of SCP-5234.


Addendum.5234-1 
During a routine research examination, SCP-5234 was caught occasionally and sporadically moving on its own seemingly with aimless intent. This included signs of twitching, and tipping its own containment box that it was stored in over at random periods. SCP-5234 now requires a box heavier than 5 pounds to make sure it is kept in one place without movement.


Addendum.5234 Incident-2 
After two confirmed weeks of continued testing, one of the researcher's earplugs was reportedly faulty. Resulting in the researcher removing all protective gear and becoming ensnared by SCP-5234 in immediate response to the whispers produced. Little matter was consumed in the time it took to contain SCP-5234. But this incident directly followed a light containment breach with the only onsite death being the former researcher.4 Internal structure of the containment cell was slightly weakened and shortly repaired after the incident. SCP-5234 was moved during repairs and soon put back into its appropriate containment cell.





Interview log.5234-1 


Interviewed:  MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood

Interviewer:  Dr. Connor

Foreword:  This log describes the events that took place in Champagne Illinois, when trying to apprehend and contain SCP-5234.

Dr. Connor:  So commander Linwood, I understand that you were the only one that made it out alive?

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood:  As a matter of fact yes, it wasn’t pretty.

Dr. Connor:  “For the record Commander, would you mind stating what happened on and after the containment of SCP-5234.”

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood: It all happened so quick. I stayed back with a few of my men to survey the town, and the rest of my team didn’t even get two god damn steps in that town before they encountered it. My team and good men they were, noticed the several amounts of growths and eyes from this man who was just laying there. Or whatever the hell it was, it wasn’t human. It jumped out of its skin and began clawing through my men taking them as it went. And as it took them my men kept on screaming, and they didn’t stop.

Dr. Connor:  Do you know why they wouldn’t stop screaming commander?

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood:  (Commander Linwood proceeds to slam his hands on the table, standing up in anger.) I don’t fucking know why. I’m still hear aren't I!? If I stuck around trying to help and console my men, I wouldn’t be alive, talking to you.

Dr. Connor:  Settle down, and please take a seat. And for the record, I don’t think you could have done much in ways of- (Dr. Conner takes a short pause.) Well, never mind let’s just continue.

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood:  (Commander Linwood sits back down, still looking pressed and infuriated.) Well when you work as long as you do for the Foundation, stuff doesn’t seem to make sense anymore.

Dr. Connor:  I understand commander but let’s not get off the subject, now you said that after a short period something crawled outside of its husk’s skin with SCP-5234 still attached. Are you able to describe exactly what you saw?

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood:  (Commander Linwood hesitates, but soon speaks up.) Something evil, whether it be the wriggling arms and legs of my men still stuck to that thing, covered in their blood and guts. And the man too, god why was he still breathing. The residents bodies still hung from the curtain, some heads and torso’s intact skin, it’s hard to remember. And the bones of the resident's arms and legs were completely exposed, no blood, no flesh, nothing. They all just lay there around that thing.

Dr. Connor:  Anything else you would like to add commander.

MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood:  The skin was beginning to corrode and dissolve off of my team, and their faces said it all. Like cattle in the slaughterhouse, so much pain and torment, yet nothing could be done at the time

Dr. Connor:  So how did you manage to subdue SCP-5234 commander, what events transpired after?

Commander Linwood:  (Commander Linwood froze, seemingly trying to process what was just asked.) Well, Dr. if I’m being honest, it took a while for backup to arrive. Like I stated earlier we opened fire on it, threw explosives, and everything we had at it. The only thing that changed was the screams of my men that went silent, the only goddamn thing we could do was put the remaining of my team out of their misery and salvage as much as we could from that thing. We shut out the town and waited until it starved itself, and then all rushed in when it was at its weakest. We had made sure it wasn’t going anywhere while we waited.

(The two paused for a short while.)

Dr. Connor:  Thank you, commander, I think that will be all

Closing Statement:  MTF Epsilon-6 commander Linwood was given the option of scheduled counseling, but declined the offer remarking. “As long as that thing is contained I can sleep well enough” and further refuses to speak on the matter at any time in the future.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Extermination record of SCP-5234:  Weapons such as scissors, hedge clippers, explosives, bullets, and fire have all proved ineffective in the extermination of SCP-5234. Starvation doesn’t seem to have any effect either, other than keeping it to a containable and safe enough size. On-going testing is still pending and any further efforts to exterminate SCP-5234 are at this time, fruitless.
